# Presence of this file makes /etc/init.d/S02swap exit immediately: no zram, no
# SD swap, no VM sysctl changes.
#
# History. Shipped present 2026-08-08 (Stage 0: 24 MB available, swap not
# needed). Removed 2026-10-03 morning when the 800x480 panel + audio pushed the
# board into page-cache thrash (MemAvailable 2-3 MB, 58 000 major faults) --
# zram fixed the thrash within seconds. Restored the same evening: with zram
# live, the hardware video decoder failed three times to allocate its CMA
# buffers ("cedrus: dma alloc of size 1048576 failed" with ~10 MB CMA free but
# no contiguous block): zsmalloc's pages are movable allocations, they land in
# the CMA pool and did not migrate out when cedrus needed the range. No video
# is worse than slow UI, so zram stays off. The thrash itself was then solved
# where it came from (float AAC decoding on a soft-float core -> aac_fixed in
# FastCarPlay; kernel diet; see docs/memory.md s4-s5).
#
# Candidates if memory gets tight again, in this order:
#   - the reserved SD partition p4 as the ONLY tier (no RAM, so no CMA
#     interference): swapon -p 10 /dev/mmcblk0p4 with vm.swappiness raised;
#     S02swap still ties p4 to a live zram and needs an SD-only mode first
#   - FastCarPlay footprint (~12 MB) and the 24 MB CMA sizing
#
# To enable zram anyway (knowing the CMA risk):  rm /etc/swap-disable && reboot
